Note that Example 4 demonstrates systems programming, bitwise operations, arrays, structures, and direct memory access.

Display text of Eathon Systems Programming Memory and Bitwise Suite end text.

Let flags be integer 42.
Let mask be integer 15.
Let masked be flags bitwise and mask.
Display masked.

Let combinedBits be flags bitwise or 128.
Display combinedBits.

Let toggledBits be flags bitwise xor 10.
Display toggledBits.

Let shiftedUp be 3 shifted left by 4.
Display shiftedUp.

Allocate array readings of 4 integers.
Store 1024 into element 0 of readings.
Store 2048 into element 1 of readings.
Store 4096 into element 2 of readings.

Load element 1 of readings into secondReading.
Display secondReading.

Allocate memory region of 64 bytes.
Write 9001 at address region offset 0.
Write 18002 at address region offset 8.
Read integer from address region offset 8 into memVal.
Display memVal.

Define structure PacketHeader with fields version as integer, payloadLength as integer.
Create pkt as PacketHeader.
Set field version of pkt to 6.
Set field payloadLength of pkt to 1480.
Get field payloadLength of pkt into pktLen.
Display pktLen.
